l  receive the certificate of completion  and this will be from the Louisiana  biomedical research network throughout  the course we will ask you to fill out  several forms that serve as pre and post  assessments we do ask that you identify  yourself we plan to use this data in a  publication later on but we also want to  provide feedback to each one of you  individually as well as to the group and  the organizers of this course and we  would like to learn from this experience  and improve our courses as well as  provide you feedback about the skills  and concepts that you've learned  throughout this course at the very end  you will be able to see the projects  that individuals came up with we will  try and separate all of the this cohort  into a number of  groups and each one will be able to  propose a project and then collaborate  on that project together with other  members of that group and this is an  example of what we did at university of  Loyola in New Orleans Loyola University  in New Orleans and some of our online  students and what they thought about  this project-based approach  now the next workshop that we are  planning to do this workshop will happen  on June 25 and 26 again here at the  computation of the Center for computer  computation and technology the CCT at  LSU in Baton Rouge and there we will  start with an overview of some of the  critical review of the approaches how to  compare different approaches when to use  different sections like pre-processing  and different mapping isoform  construction and and expression level  quantification methods we will talk  about differential gene expression how  to compare fold change between so how to  quantify change and see whether change  is statistically significant between two  groups and then how to use machine  learning methods to classify different  samples and finally at the end when you  start learning about the projects and we  will start working on preparing ideas  for analysis of the data and 